{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "שם ה' נקרא", :translit "shem H' nikra", :gloss "the name of YHWH is called"} {:he "של תפילין", :translit "shel tefillin", :gloss "of tefillin"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "שם ה' נקרא", :spells "שי\"ן"}], :frame {:text "The initial letters of 'שם ה' נקרא' (Deuteronomy 28:10) spell שי\"ן, which the Ba'al HaTurim reads as an abbreviation for 'של תפילין,' linking the verse's promise that all nations will see God's name called upon Israel to the observance of tefillin.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 28:10"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ויראו ממך", :translit "v'yare'u mimeka", :gloss "and they shall fear you"} {:he "והותירך ה'", :translit "v'hotirkha H'", :gloss "and HaShem will prolong you"} {:he "אדני עליהם יחיו", :translit "Adonai aleihem yichyu", :gloss "Adonai, upon them they shall live"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Contextual adjacency: verse 28:10 is followed directly by 28:11's promise of prolonged days, linked to tefillin."}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'אדני עליהם יחיו' (Isaiah 38:16) is read homiletically: 'Adonai' recalls the divine name on the tefillin, and 'upon them they shall live' teaches that tefillin confer longevity. The adjacent verse 'והותירך ה' בטוב' (Deuteronomy 28:11) — promising prolonged days immediately after 'וראו כל עמי הארץ כי שם ה' נקרא עליך' (Deuteronomy 28:10) — is thus explained: the nations fear Israel because of the tefillin, and in their merit God prolongs Israel's days.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 28:10" "Deuteronomy 28:11" "Isaiah 38:16"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "שם ה' נקרא", :spells "שי\"ן", :letters ["ש" "ה" "נ"], :by :selah, :order :mismatch} {:kind :other, :note "Contextual adjacency: verse 28:10 is followed directly by 28:11's promise of prolonged days, linked to tefillin.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:39:58.604052176Z", :m